Differences Between Multiple Inheritance and Multilevel Inheritance

------------Multiple Inheritance------------------------------------------Mulitlevel Inheritance-------------------------

Definition	•	A derived class inherits from more than one base class.	•	A derived class inherits from another derived class.
Number of Base Classes	•	Two or more base classes for one derived class.	•	One base class, then another derived class inherits from it, and so on.
Class Hierarchy Shape	•	Diamond or multiple parents to one child.	•	Linear hierarchy (a chain of inheritance).
Example Use Case	•	Combining features from different classes.	•	Extending functionality step-by-step.
Complexity	•	Can cause ambiguity if base classes have same method names (requires resolution).	•	Simpler and straightforward.

